  "scope": "# 34569d6118b3 \u2014 review-42426b9aefb72b0d\nSource: generator 4.0.0, SHA256 f61a4b88290f3c23cb001c42ae36f4fad9f9fa0f3ae3e491efbd9f3a26c6f409; rule e2b81b5e525c.\nChange: missing parametric extension \u2192 proposed forward/reverse template binding and optional horizontal mask reflection.\nCanonical generator, canonical Racket, authorities and approval bytes are unchanged; default program is byte-exact.\nVerified: 14 prototype tests and 15 sparse-packager tests passed; all 29 focused tests executed, no skips.\nLabels: four episodes \u00d7 (3 demos + 4 distinct queries), 112 Racket selected/rival predictions; all 16 queries identified from demonstrations.\nTeaching: reject ambiguous compact-only first demos; retain a concrete reverse+mirror ambiguity counterexample in the focused suite.\nTool: stdlib sparse package adapter invokes the unchanged issued builder/validator; full-fixture ZIP output is byte-identical.\nTickets: one Racket-backed border-only witness retained; older two-stage-summary request reproduced as already implemented.\nLimits: proposed variants only; four declared rivals; bounded sampling; Linux atomic export; no production battery or new approval.\nReplay: official fresh runtime-closure patch replay passed for all six changed paths; final source patch is byte-identical to the replayed candidate.\nDisposition: routine task-local prototype; optional packaging helper remains a maintainer-reviewed proposal.",
